        "summary": "The university warns that researchers remain responsible and accountable for AI-generated content and that reliance on unverified AI material can expose authors to findings of academic and research misconduct if fabrication, falsification, or plagiarism are present. It also states that using AI in the peer review process is a breach of confidentiality and cites NIH’s prohibition for NIH peer review, noting that even using AI to draft or polish critiques is considered a confidentiality breach.",
