        "summary": "The academic integrity policy treats using unauthorized aids in examinations or other academic exercises submitted for evaluation as cheating, and also includes work generated through unsanctioned and/or undocumented AI assistance as an academic integrity violation. The policy does not separately define exam-specific AI rules beyond these general academic integrity standards.",
        "evidence": "Cheating is the fraudulent or dishonest presentation of work. Cheating includes but is not limited to:\n* the use or attempted use of unauthorized aids in examinations or other academic exercises submitted for evaluation;\n\n* work generated through unsanctioned and/or undocumented artificial intelligence (A.I.) assistance.",
