        "evidence": "In all cases, students must acknowledge any use of generative AI in writing or via citation at the time of assignment submission, as required by university policy.\nContent within an assignment submission that has been generated by Artificial Intelligence must be properly cited and revised for clarity, correctness, and audience appropriateness.\nTier 2 – Limited (with Disclosure) -- Examples: AI may be used to check grammar. Students must disclose how AI was used.\nIf so, students must confirm the approval of their committee for AI use and must document their use of AI in footnotes and in a statement in their bibliography/references. The statement will explain where and how AI was used, and it will include a citation such as:  Chat GPT-4, month, day, year [of query], “text of query.” Generated using [link].\n• When AI tools are used to assist with academic work, students must include a brief note of disclosure indicating when and how the tools were used. For example:\n\"Portions of this paper were assisted using ChatGPT on July 7, 2025 for outlining and grammar checking. All written content reflects the student's own original work.\"\n• When AI tools are used to assist theses/dissertations, manuscripts, posters, or presentations, students must include a brief note of disclosure indicating when and how the tools were used.",
        "sourceUrls": [
          "https://www.memphis.edu/fcbe/resources/policies/ai.php",
          "https://www.memphis.edu/fcbe/pdfs/fcbe-ai-policy-2025.pdf",
          "https://www.memphis.edu/um3d/resources/genaisyllabus.php",
          "https://www.memphis.edu/music/about/studentresources/graduate_handbook2020/gradhandbook3.0.php",
          "https://www.memphis.edu/psychology/graduate/pdfs/school-psych-doctoral-handbook25-26.pdf"
        ],
        "defined": true
