        "evidence": "While collaboration is encouraged, students must not share copies of their code for programming assignments. Any violation will NOT be tolerated, resulting in a failing grade for the course, and will be reported to the Associate Dean of ENS as per college policy.\n\nAcceptable use of AI tools:\n  * Brainstorming and conceptualizing ideas\n  * Troubleshooting bugs\n  * Check and refine syntax (i.e., in writing and programming)\n\nUnacceptable use of AI tools:\n\n  * Completing entire assignments\n  * Resource gathering (AI will cite made-up sources)\n  * Asset development\n\nNote: This is not a campus-wide policy and only applies to this course.",
