        "domain": "Institutional & Administrative",
        "summary": "Cal Poly supports faculty and staff use of AI through training resources, syllabus guidance, and tools for course and administrative applications. An employee toolkit provides best practices, advising staff to use AI as a tool rather than a replacement, to fact-check AI-generated content, and to adhere to data security standards. The university is also developing formal guidelines for faculty and student use.",
        "evidence": "The guidance and best practices below are intended to give you a starting point as you consider using AI in your work... Use AI as a tool, not a replacement for your own work... Fact-check and verify information provided by AI tools... Do not enter Level 1 data into any AI tool... The Cal Poly AI Core Values and Syllabus Statements web page provides Cal Poly instructional faculty practical tools for integrating statements about AI usage into their course syllabi... Yes! ChatGPT Edu allows for creating and sharing custom GPTs—such as tools tailored to specific courses or administrative needs. ... Provide guidelines to distinguish ethical and unethical uses of GAI by both faculty and students.",
