        "domain": "Research",
        "summary": "UT San Antonio does not provide a general research data-analysis rule, but it does prohibit uploading novel grant content into AI tools and warns about confidentiality risks in research review contexts. The research guidance specifically references AI being used to analyze and create peer reviews as prohibited by the sponsoring agency example it cites.",
        "evidence": "▪ Never upload your grant application (novel idea) into any AI tool as then it will be in the public domain and accessible by others.\nFor example, the National Institutes of Health (NIH) has prohibited scientific peer reviewers from employing natural language processors, large language models, or other generative Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies to analyze and create peer reviews for grant applications and R&D contract proposals.\nThis limitation is in place due to concerns about maintaining confidentiality, as these AI tools lack guarantees regarding the handling, storage, access, and future use of data.",
