        "summary": "UTA’s research guidance allows generative AI to be used in research-related writing such as proposal preparation, progress reports, and manuscripts, but users remain responsible for accuracy, authenticity, and integrity. Disclosure is required when appropriate or when required by the journal or sponsor. The guidance is framed for the UTA research community rather than as a blanket ban.",
        "evidence": "Uses of GAI in research may involve proposal preparation, progress reports, data/statistical analysis, graphic generation, etc.\n\nProposers are responsible for the accuracy and authenticity of their proposal submission in consideration for merit review, including content developed with the assistance of generative AI tools.\n\nDisclose use of GAI tools when appropriate or required (e.g., a journal that will accept a manuscript developed using GAI, provided such use is disclosed).",
