      "U3": {
        "classification_name": "Learning & Study Assistance",
        "domain": "Teaching & Learning",
        "summary": "The university permits AI as a learning aid and encourages responsible use for tutoring, feedback, studying, and general learning support. Students may use AI tools for personalized learning and research assistance, but they are told to verify information, rely on authoritative sources, and check with professors when assignment-related use is involved.",
        "evidence": "Use AI tools in a way that is consistent with enhancing and supporting your own and others’ agency, creativity, connection, and critical thinking.  AI tools may be used to augment these qualities but should not be used to supplant them.\nGenerative AI can be used to help students with learning. It has the potential to provide students with personalized learning experience on any topics. Below are some ideas about using AI as a personal tutor.\nTimely feedback is essential for student learning. Although not a substitute for instructor feedback, with well-constructed prompts, AI-generated feedback can help students improve their work.\nGenerative AI has the potential to be a personal tutor for students. For AI to be an effective tutor, an interactive dialogue between students and AI is needed. A well-crafted prompt helps create a dialogue between students and AI, guiding students through learning. Although students may use any generative AI tools, AI Tutoring Pro is a tool specifically designed for this purpose.\nAI tools can assist in the research processby:\n  * brainstorming ideas for topics, research questions, and research designs\n  * searching for sources or generating search strategies such as keywords, phrases, and concepts for searching\n  * summarizing or simplifying large quantities of text for aid in literature reviews\n  * analyzing and visualizing data to identify themes, trends, and other patterns\n  * translating information into other languages\n  * improving writing through editing, proofreading, and clarifying ideas\nTo address these limitations, you can use some of the following strategies:\n  * Confirm the information you get from a generative AI tool by researching it in authoritative sources.",
        "sourceUrls": [
          "https://www.unr.edu/ai/students/guidelines",
          "https://www.unr.edu/teaching-excellence/teaching-resources/generative-ai",
          "https://www.unr.edu/ai/students/research-tasks"
        ],
        "defined": true
      },
