        "summary": "The official university policy treats use of generative AI during examinations, tests, and quizzes as cheating unless the instructor expressly allows it in the syllabus or the specific assessment. CTL sample language also includes course policies that forbid AI use for evaluated work outside specifically authorized contexts.",
        "evidence": "\"Using notes, textbooks or other information, or content generated by internet-based generative artificial intelligence programs (GAI), in examinations, tests and quizzes, except as expressly permitted by the instructor in the syllabus, examination, test, or quiz;\"\n\n\"There are situations and contexts within this course where you will be asked to use AI tools to explore how they can be used.  Outside of those circumstances, you are discouraged from using AI tools to generate content (text, video, audio, images) that will end up in any student work (assignments, activities, responses, etc) that is part of your evaluation in this course.\"",
