        "domain": "Institutional & Administrative",
        "summary": "CSU actively supports faculty and staff AI use through centralized training, workshops, and a faculty AI literacy certificate. For teaching practice, instructors are told to set and reiterate academic integrity expectations, and the university offers resources on authentic assessment and integrating AI into teaching and research.",
        "evidence": "This website helps faculty, staff, and students with centralized information on AI-related training, events, research, and resources. We are connecting the campus community to workshops, events, tools, and best practices for integrating AI into teaching and research.\nThe Office of Instructional Excellence and Michael Schwartz Library have partnered to develop a certificate course for faculty to help understand Generative AI and its use. This course is completely asynchronous and can be completed at the faculty member's own pace.\nExploring authentic assessments that align well with the presence and use of generative AI and crafting meaningful learning experiences that remain relevant and effective in an AI-enhanced classroom.\nInclude a statement on academic integrity in your syllabus.\nCommunicate and reiterate your expectations regarding academic integrity throughout the semester.",
