        "domain": "Teaching & Learning",
        "summary": "The university does not state an AI-specific exam rule in the provided sources, but its academic dishonesty policy prohibits using electronic equipment or information during examinations when unauthorized, and it also allows professors to set special exam rules. This means exam-related tool use is governed by general cheating rules and professor-designated restrictions rather than a separate AI policy.",
        "evidence": "Cheating is the act of deceiving, which includes such acts as receiving or communicating or receiving information from another during an examination, looking at another's examination (during the exam), using notes when prohibited during examinations, using electronic equipment to receive or communicate information during examinations, using any unauthorized electronic equipment during examinations, obtaining information about the questions or answers for an examination prior to the administering of the examination or whatever else is deemed contrary to the rules of fairness, including special rules designated by the professor in the course.",
