        "evidence": "Remember that while AI can be a valuable aid in the grant writing process, human expertise, creativity, and domain knowledge remain essential. Use AI tools as complementary resources to enhance your proposal, but always review and tailor the content to meet the specific requirements and objectives of the funding opportunity and your research in STEM education.\nAdditionally, be transparent about any AI assistance you use in your proposal, as some grant agencies may have specific guidelines regarding AI-generated content.\nCaution is also in place when using AI for literature review and research background; check whether the references are real citations and not fake ones or that the information isn't outdated, thus not reflecting current knowledge in a particular field or discipline.",
