        "evidence": "Researchers must consider ethical implications, obtain necessary approvals, and avoid bias in data or algorithm use. Ensure that AI research complies with institutional review board (IRB) protocols, ethical standards, and sponsor imposed contractual requirements. Researchers must consult with any intended journals and their editors on their policies and/or standards on the use of AI for what is allowed, not allowed, and required for publication.\n\nWhen AI systems interact directly with individuals, e.g., research participants, students, faculty, or staff, informed consent is required. This includes clear communication of the purpose, scope, and potential impacts of data collection and analysis. Individuals should have the option to opt out without facing negative consequences.",
