        "summary": "When instructors permit AI use, disclosure and citation requirements may apply at the course level rather than through a single fixed university-wide rule. Students may be required to submit a declaration describing the tools used and the extent of use, and the working group guidance says instructors should specify how AI-generated content must be cited and how it will be evaluated.",
        "evidence": "When use of generative AI is permitted for course assignments, the student may be required to provide a declaration outlining the tools used and the extent of their use in each submission.\nIf an instructor allows the inclusion of AI-generated content in student submissions, it is helpful to specify exactly how such content must be cited and how such content will be considered when evaluating student performance.\nFor information on citation consult, MSU Libraries’ Citation Guides at https://guides.library.msstate.edu/citationguides.",
