        "summary": "The college requires research to follow responsible and ethical conduct standards, mandates oversight for human and animal research, and provides reporting channels for suspected research misconduct. However, the provided sources do not state a specific AI policy for grant proposals, IRB applications, or ethics declarations.",
        "evidence": "The Research Compliance Office at Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences provides access to a variety of resources and training programs to ensure all individuals engaged in research at the College adhere to the highest standards for responsible and ethical conduct.\n\nComments, concerns, requests, and reports regarding suspected compliance issues, including research misconduct, may be made by contacting the Research Compliance Office at (518) 694-7238.\n\nAt Albany College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences, all human subject research (regardless of whether funded) must be reviewed and approved by the IRB before initiation.",
