        "evidence": "Any action that, in the opinion of the instructor, would unfairly advance a student’s academic performance or would unfairly limit or impede another student’s academic performance may be considered a violation of academic integrity.\n\nHelping or attempting to help another student commit an act of academic dishonesty, including assistance with an assignment, quiz, test or exam, is considered a violation of integrity.\n\nPlagiarism includes, but is not limited to, the following:\n• Obtaining or attempting to obtain all or part of a term paper, or other assignment, by copying all or part of another person’s work.\n• Submitting as one’s own work a paper, or any part of a paper, purchased or otherwise obtained from an Internet source, another individual, or a company or organization that sells term papers or similar materials.",
