        "summary": "The college prohibits entering sensitive or confidential information, including non-public research data, into AI tools that are not authorized by the college. It also states that AI-generated data analysis from raw data, survey data, or dashboards must be treated as content for which the user remains responsible and must review before sharing or publication.",
        "evidence": "Safeguard Sensitive, Confidential, and Restricted Data: Do not enter sensitive or confidential information, including non-public research data and student and/or employee data, into AI tools not authorized by the college for such usage. Information shared with third-party AI tools could be exposed to unauthorized parties.\nData analysis generated from raw data, survey data and or data dashboards\nResponsible Use: You are responsible for any content you produce or publish, including AI-generated content. AI-generated content can be inaccurate, misleading, or entirely fabricated (sometimes called “hallucinations”), or may unintentionally contain copyrighted, sensitive, or even confidential material. AI-generated content can also contribute to misinformation. Always review your AI-generated content before publication or sharing.",
