        "domain": "Institutional & Administrative",
        "summary": "ATU does not require employees to use generative AI, and employee use must stay within approved scope. Faculty and staff using AI in professional or official work must disclose AI assistance in professional outputs, and any AI-assisted workflows that materially affect people or decisions require human oversight and human final authority.",
        "evidence": "ATU will set clear boundaries for what university activities AI is allowed to support and what it is not allowed to support. AI may be used only within that approved scope. ATU will not require employees to use generative AI to perform their duties, and any required student use of AI must be clearly disclosed and include a reasonable alternative when appropriate.\n• Individual ATU employees will disclose their use of AI assistance in any professional publication, presentation, or product created at ATU or using ATU-licensed materials.\nIf AI helps produce an output, the person using it is accountable for what it says and how it is used.\nIn accordance with Arkansas Act 848 of 2025, any AI or automated decision tool used by the university must support a policy that ensures a human employee or authorized designee makes any final decision, regardless of AI recommendations.",
