        "summary": "For student coursework, generative AI use is not uniformly permitted or prohibited across all classes. Students must follow the specific instructor's directions for each assignment, and using AI in a way not authorized by the instructor can be treated as plagiarism.",
        "evidence": "The use of generative artificial intelligence tools (GAITs), including ChatGPT, to complete assignments may be considered plagiarism or cheating. If your course instructor permits the use of GAITs for an assignment, then using a GAIT is not plagiarism.\n\nThe course instructor’s directions should indicate whether using a GAIT is or is not permitted for a specific assignment.",
