        "domain": "Research",
        "summary": "The university’s academic integrity policy requires proper acknowledgment of sources and treats presenting someone else’s words or ideas as one’s own as plagiarism. However, it does not define a specific policy on AI use for drafting or editing research manuscripts.",
        "evidence": "Proper acknowledgment of ideas and sources is central to academic honesty.\n\nPlagiarism is the intentional or unintentional presentation of someone else’s words, ideas or data as one’s own work.\n\nIf the work of another is used, acknowledgment of the original source must be made through a recognized documentation practice.",
