        "evidence": "AI literacy at AIU goes beyond basic technical exposure. It encompasses a comprehensive understanding of how artificial intelligence systems work, how they are applied across sectors, and how they should be used responsibly, ethically, and critically.\n\nThe initiative integrates AI literacy into academic programs through interdisciplinary coursework, hands-on learning experiences, and applied projects aligned with real-world use cases. Students are introduced to key concepts such as data-driven decision-making, generative AI, automation, and AI ethics, while also developing critical thinking skills to assess limitations, bias, and societal impact.\n\nAIU’s approach emphasizes responsible and ethical AI use, ensuring graduates understand not only what AI can do, but also what it should do.",
