      "U12": {
        "classification_name": "University AI Governance & Strategy",
        "domain": "Institutional & Administrative",
        "summary": "Augusta University has an institution-wide AI framework focused on responsible adoption, data protection, academic integrity, transparency, and accountability. The university presents institutional guidelines for the whole community and identifies five core principles to guide AI use. The sources do not name a formal AI committee or detailed roadmap.",
        "evidence": "Artificial intelligence is transforming how we learn, teach, and research. At Augusta University, we are committed to leveraging these powerful tools responsibly to expand the boundaries of higher education.\n\nArtificial intelligence is reshaping the landscape of higher education, redefining the ways we teach, conduct research, and collaborate. Augusta University is dedicated to embracing these advancements with a focus on responsibility—fostering innovation while strictly safeguarding university data and upholding the highest standards of academic integrity.\nThese institutional guidelines serve as a framework for our entire community, ensuring that students, faculty, and staff can explore the potential of AI within a secure and ethical environment.\nOur core approach is built on five fundamental principles that ensure AI use aligns with our values of academic excellence and ethical conduct:\n  * Protect University Data: Always classify your data before entering it into any system.\n  * Prefer Approved Services: Use tools reviewed by AU IT for any non-public data.\n  * Verify All AI Outputs: AI can \"hallucinate\" or create fabricated information; always review results before use.\n  * Be Transparent: Disclose your use of AI whenever required by instructors or publishers.\n  * You Remain Responsible: You are ultimately accountable for any work products or decisions produced with AI assistance.",
        "sourceUrls": [
          "https://www.augusta.edu/ai/index.php"
        ],
        "defined": true
      }
