        "summary": "AI use during exams and assessments is not uniformly allowed; it depends on whether the faculty member has authorized it. Ball State’s syllabus language treats use of unauthorized AI tools during academic work as an integrity violation, and faculty are advised to specify expectations about generative AI for the course or specific assignments.",
        "evidence": "* Using resources not authorized by the faculty member (including devices, AI tools, hidden notes, and open books)\n* Sharing answers with others during exams (passing notes, texting, whispering, gesturing)\n* Discussing exam questions and answers with students who have not taken the exam.\nMake explicit on your syllabi and discuss with students your expectations regarding actions that are acceptable vs. not (and why), especially regarding using classmates' work, collaborating with peers, and using generative AI (for the entire course or for specific assignments).",
