        "domain": "Academic Integrity",
        "summary": "Ball State routes suspected AI-related misconduct through its academic integrity process rather than stating a university-wide AI detection rule. Faculty are encouraged to address suspected AI misuse consistently and care, and formal disputes proceed through the Student Academic Ethics Hearing process. Unauthorized AI use is identified as an academic integrity violation in the syllabus guidance.",
        "evidence": "Addressing Suspected AI Misuse with Consistency and Care\nIf the student disagrees with the accusation or resolution discussed in the private conference or seeks to appeal the academic ethics violation, the incident will be handled with the formal resolution process of a Student Academic Ethics Hearing.\nAll work conducted and/or submitted in this course should reflect your own ideas and demonstrate your current knowledge, abilities, and skills. Therefore, generative AI should not be used to complete any portion of the assignment(s). Doing so constitutes a violation of Ball State University's Student Academic Ethics Policy.",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.bsu.edu/about/administrativeoffices/vice-provost/faculty-services/professional-development/academic-integrity-and-ai", "https://www.bsu.edu/about/administrativeoffices/information-technology/services/ai-initiatives/academic-integrity", "https://www.bsu.edu/about/administrativeoffices/vice-provost/faculty-services/syllabus-resources"],
