      "U12": {
        "classification_name": "University AI Governance & Strategy",
        "domain": "Institutional & Administrative",
        "summary": "Ball State has an institutional AI initiative centered on ethical, responsible, and impactful AI integration across education, research, and operations. Its AI guidelines are described as living guidance, grounded in university values and commitments to academic integrity, human creativity and critical thinking, accessibility, minimizing harm, and ethical considerations. The university also promotes resources, training, approved tools, and campus initiatives to support adoption.",
        "evidence": "These are living guidelines and are continuously updated as new information is received. All information is subject to change. These guidelines were last updated on February 12, 2025.\nAs Cardinals, we are committed to fostering an ethical approach to AI that aligns with our enduring values:\n* Excellence. We commit to using AI in ways that align with and uphold our Academic Integrity Policy.\n* Innovation. We commit to responsible AI experimentation and implementation to enhance creativity, learning, and research.\n* Integrity. We commit to upholding human creativity and critical thinking with our AI usage, avoiding misuse.\n* Inclusiveness. We commit to developing and using AI in accessible and equitable ways, designing and testing with safety as a priority.\n* Social responsibility. We commit to minimizing harm, maintaining rigorous standards, and prioritizing ethical considerations when using AI.\nFrom foundational courses to specialized workshops, our resources provide practical skills for leveraging AI tools in academia, research, and beyond. Explore guides, tutorials, and certification opportunities to build expertise in this rapidly evolving field, ensuring that our university remains at the forefront of ethical, responsible, and impactful AI integration.\nDiscover the university's innovative AI projects and initiatives driving research, education, and community impact in artificial intelligence.",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.bsu.edu/about/administrativeoffices/information-technology/services/ai-initiatives/ai-guidelines", "https://www.bsu.edu/about/administrativeoffices/information-technology/services/ai-initiatives"],
        "defined": true
      },
