        "evidence": "Applies to (check all that apply):\nFaculty___X_ Staff____ Students ___X_\nThe College requires all courses to have an AI syllabus statement(s) that can range from prohibited to no restrictions. It is the instructor’s decision on how AI is permitted in courses.\nIt is the policy of Baltimore City Community College that the instructor must define acceptable use of online learning support platforms based on the following AI Course Syllabus statement guidelines:\nChairman Schmoke asked whether the faculty would decide if Artificial Intelligence would be prohibited in a given class and disclose that information in the syllabus. Dr. Hill responded that yes, each faculty would make that decision.",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.bccc.edu/fs/resource-manager/view/70cdfd9d-b785-4d6f-a755-7aa6a4e7edfd", "https://www.bccc.edu/cms/lib/MD02000050/Centricity/Domain/53/BCCC%20Board%20of%20Trustees%20Meeting%20May%2015%202024%20-%20Open%20Session.pdf"],
        "defined": true
