        "summary": "The seminary requires graduate students to develop research and writing ability at the graduate level and trains them in formal research paper formatting and evidence-based argumentation. It also requires research papers in the curriculum, and Master of Divinity students must submit an exemplary research paper in the portfolio.",
        "evidence": "Research papers must develop a line of argumentation that interacts withother viewpoints and uses evidence to defend the view adopted.\n\nAll master's programs require students to \"evidence an ability to do theological research and writingat a graduate level\" (Master's Program Goal 3).Toensure this,FBTS requires all students to take the Theological Research course at the beginning of their program. This course trains students how to conduct graduate-level research in better scholarly resources. It alsotrains them how to formulate cogent arguments and how to useevidence in theological research. Finally, the course trains students in how to properly format a formal research paper. These research skills are reinforced throughout the curricula as professors require research papers in various classes. Master of Divinity students must submit an exemplary research paper as an artifact in the M.Div. portfolio, which demonstrates their ability to research and formulate a cogentargument.",
