        "evidence": "So, running a sermon, book review, or research paper through a program that assists the writer in finding grammatical errors to be corrected is acceptable.\nSecond, is “Generative” AI that creates a sermon or paper for an individual. This seems to be unacceptable when it comes to preparing sermons or school assignments.\nOf course, a research paper “by Philip Attebery” likely includes quotations or ideas he found from other authors or perhaps content produced by Generative AI. In such cases, those quotations should be properly cited in footnotes or endnotes as belonging originally to another author or source. If I submit a paper that is generated by AI or copied from another author, I cannot honestly declare it was written “by Philip Attebery.”",
