        "summary": "Bard’s university-level policy is that students may not use generative AI for coursework unless an instructor expressly permits it. Faculty set the rules for each course and assignment through the syllabus and course materials, and course-specific policies govern academic integrity expectations.",
        "evidence": "Students may not use GenAI tools for coursework unless expressly permitted.\nFaculty are to determine and communicate in each course syllabus and accompanying course materials the degree to which they allow students to use GenAI tools, if at all.\nWhen it comes to matters of academic integrity, the instructor’s GenAI policy defines the expectations for that course.",
