        "evidence": "Faculty are to determine and communicate in each course syllabus and accompanying course materials the degree to which they allow students to use GenAI tools, if at all.\nFor example, how could you write code to reorganize your data for your senior project in a particular way?\nWhen appropriate, and as guided by your professor, you might practice some of these uses in your courses, including your senior project.\nIf you’re using ChatGPT to help you solve a coding challenge for your senior project, for example, you will know whether the code works by actually trying to use it.\nIt goes without saying that it is not okay to use any generative AI tool to write code for you.",
