        "domain": "Academic Integrity",
        "summary": "Bard requires acknowledgement and/or citation of generative AI use for academic integrity purposes whenever AI is used in accordance with instructor guidelines. If an instructor does not specify a citation format, students must be transparent about how AI contributed to their work or understanding and should ask the instructor if they are unsure.",
        "evidence": "Use of GenAI tools require acknowledgement and/or citation for academic integrity.\nEven when used in accordance with guidelines provided by the instructor, students must acknowledge and/or cite GenAI contributions in keeping with the Bard Plagiarism and Academic Dishonesty Policy. If the instructor does not provide specific instructions related to the citation of GenAI as a source of information, then students are expected to err on the side of transparency, making clear how GenAI has contributed to their work or to their understanding of course materials.\nIt is the student’s responsibility to clarify questions with their instructor regarding the use and citation of GenAI in academic coursework.",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.bard.edu/wwwmedia/files/7137089/2/Bard%20College%20Policy%20on%20Academic%20Use%20of%20Generative%20Artificial%20Intelligence.pdf"],
