        "summary": "Barry University explicitly supports faculty and staff use of AI for teaching and administrative work. The university lists uses such as generating course materials, automating grading and feedback, proofreading documents, and other productivity tasks, and provides an AI assistant quick-start for faculty and staff.",
        "evidence": "Brought to you by the Barry AI Enablement Office to help faculty and staff personalize AI tools for faster, safer work.\n  * Generating course materials & syllabi updates\n  * Automating grading & personalized feedback\n  * Automating meeting minutes & action items\n  * Reviewing & proofreading emails, documents, presentations\nEducators must be equipped with the skills to harness AI effectively—leveraging it to enhance student engagement, streamline administrative tasks, and foster creativity in the classroom. Faculty will need to learn how to incorporate AI tools into their pedagogy, rethink assessment strategies in an era of generative AI, and ensure students develop the digital literacy required for the workforce of tomorrow.",
