        "evidence": "Protecting University Data, especially Sensitive Information, is a critical legal and ethical responsibility at Barry University. Strict adherence to the WISP, Responsible Use of Artificial Intelligence Tools Policy, ACUP, and the Agreement to Maintain the Privacy and Security of University Data is required when handling such information with AI.\nYou MUST get Information Security Office (ISO) authorization before putting any University Data (especially sensitive data) into any AI tool.\nOnly use AI tools that have been vetted and explicitly approved by the Barry University ISO.\n  * Using unvetted or public AI models (like free versions of ChatGPT, etc.) with University Data is strictly prohibited.\n#### Tools\nMicrosoft Copilot, OpenAI Teams, Fireflies.ai, Grammarly.\n#### Sensitive data only in Copilot\nIf sensitive data appears elsewhere, stop and say “Use Copilot.”\n#### Gemini\nUse only for non‑sensitive work unless specifically approved.\n#### Follow accessibility and privacy policies\nAvoid PHI and FERPA‑protected content unless authorized.\n  * Microsoft Copilot – Approved for all University data, including PHI (Paid license required)\n  * Gemini – Approved for University data excluding PHI\n  * OpenAI Teams (ChatGPT) – Approved for University data excluding PHI\n  * OpenAI Free (ChatGPT) – Not approved for University Data\n  * Claude – Approved for University data excluding PHI\n  * Fireflies.ai – Approved for meeting transcription only\n  * Grammarly – Approved for text proofreading only\n  * Adobe Firefly, Canva, Pixlr, Microsoft Designer – Approved for image/video editing only (Not for sensitive data)\n  * Perplexity – Approved for research and web search (Not for sensitive data)",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.barry.edu/en/ai-hub/data-protection/", "https://www.barry.edu/en/ai-hub/ai-assistant/", "https://www.barry.edu/en/information-security-office/ai-use-cases/"],
