        "evidence": "Bates provides all faculty, students, and staff with user accounts for accessing and using Google Workspace for Education, including G-Mail, Google Docs, and Gemini.\n\nGoogle’s multimodal AI model, which can “understand and reason across different types of information including text, images, audio, video, and code.” Gemini is available for all Bates users from the Bates Google Workspace\n\n  * Writing tools – Summarize text, proof your writing, and experiment with tone.\n\nThe Environmental Studies Program recognizes that Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Large Language Models (LLMs) are premised on extraction and theft — of water, land, energy, creativity, and intellectual property. Generative AI and LLMs thus profoundly threaten the fundamental ideals of social and environmental justice. Furthermore, critical thinking is a foundational skill that all liberal arts students should develop, and the use of LLMs may precisely inhibit such critical thought.",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.bates.edu/curricular-research-computing/ai-bates/", "https://www.bates.edu/curricular-research-computing/ai-bates/resources/gen-ai/", "https://www.bates.edu/environment/ai-policy/"],
