        "evidence": "Use of Artificial Intelligence (AI): The use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools and platforms must comply with all college data protection guidelines and data classification rules. Restricted data may only be processed or analyzed using AI tools that have undergone a formal review and received explicit approval based on their privacy and security protections.\n\nThis review is conducted by Information & Library Services’ Office of Information Security; requests for review should be submitted via the ILS Helpdesk. Users are responsible for verifying that any AI tool employed meets these college-approved standards before using it with Restricted data.\n\nUsing AI with Restricted Data: Restricted data (including PII, FERPA-protected records, financial information, and health data) must not be processed or analyzed using any AI tool unless that specific tool has undergone formal review and received explicit approval from the Information & Library Services’ Office of Information Security, as outlined in the main policy section. Unauthorized AI tools must never be used with Restricted data.\n\nGeneral Use Cases: AI tools not formally approved for Restricted data may still be suitable for tasks involving Public or Internal (non-Restricted) data, such as refining teaching materials, analyzing publicly available datasets, or composing non-confidential documents. However, whenever possible, using college-approved tools is preferred even for these tasks to ensure alignment with institutional standards.",
