        "summary": "Bay Atlantic University prohibits students from using generative AI to draft or write academic work unless a faculty member explicitly directs its use. The policy applies to students studying on campus or online, and violations are treated as cheating with escalating academic penalties.",
        "evidence": "Studentsstudying on-campus or online are expected to submit original work using their own ideas and words.\nConsistent with the University’s expectations on academic integrity and student conduct, the use of Generative AI tools, unless explicitly directed by a faculty member, to draft or write any academic work is considered cheating.\nStudents who plagiarize or use generative Ai will face the following:\n1st Offense: The student will receive a zero (0) on the assignment.\n2nd Offense: The student will fail the class.",
