        "domain": "Academic Integrity",
        "summary": "Unauthorized AI use is treated as academic dishonesty and may trigger the college's academic misconduct process. Faculty are instructed to address suspected misuse using the academic dishonesty procedure, and sanctions can range from assignment penalties to course failure and possible suspension or expulsion depending on severity or repetition.",
        "evidence": "Use of GenAI in violation of this policy may constitute academic dishonesty. Any misuse should be addressed in accordance with Beaufort County Community College’s academic honesty and student conduct procedures.\n\nIf a student violates the established guidelines for using AI in coursework or assignments, faculty should address the matter in accordance with the College's Academic Dishonesty Procedure.\n\nAcademic dishonesty includes, but is not limited to cheating, plagiarism, use of AI generators when not explicitly authorized by the course instructor, fabrication, and facilitating or helping others to be academically dishonest.\n\nA student who commits an act of academic dishonesty, including a first offense, may receive one or more of the following sanctions at the discretion of the instructor:\n1. Requirement to repeat the assignment.\n2. Grade reduction on the assignment.\n3. Grade of “F” on the assignment.\n4. Grade of “F” in the course.\n\nIf the student commits another violation of academic dishonesty, if the first offense is so egregious as to warrant more severe action, or if the student is in a Selective/Competitive Admission Program (which may have additional consequences), the matter may be referred for disciplinary action up to and including suspension or expulsion.",
