        "domain": "Institutional & Administrative",
        "summary": "Faculty and staff may use generative AI to support instruction and work, but not as a replacement for professional judgment. Faculty must set and communicate course-level AI rules, and all AI-generated work products must be reviewed, edited, and verified by a human before use.",
        "evidence": "Beaufort County Community College supports the thoughtful and responsible use of generative artificial intelligence (“GenAI”) by students, faculty, and staff to enhance learning, support instruction, and increase efficiency in work.\n\nEmployees may use GenAI to support or enhance work and student learning but may not use it in place of performing their own responsibilities.\n\nFaculty have the authority to determine whether and to what extent students may use GenAI in all aspects of course assignments and assessments, unless specifically restricted under this policy.\n\nFaculty should be clear with students about when and how they may use GenAI in coursework.\n\nAll work products developed with the use of GenAI must be reviewed, edited, and verified by a human to ensure accuracy, completeness, and quality.",
