        "summary": "Bellevue College states that AI use in coursework is governed at the course level. Students must follow each instructor’s specific AI expectations for graded work, including whether AI is allowed and what consequences apply for inappropriate use.",
        "evidence": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) can serve as a valuable tool for learning and completing academic tasks. Bellevue College has established rules and guidelines to support the responsible use of AI in coursework. Individual classes and instructors will define their specific expectations regarding AI use, including whether it is permitted, the rationale for its use or restriction, and the consequences of inappropriate use. Students are responsible for reviewing and clarifying their instructor’s AI policy.",
