        "domain": "Teaching & Learning",
        "summary": "Bellevue College presents AI as a learning support tool for students and describes it as useful for learning and academic tasks. The college also provides faculty development encouraging classroom uses of AI to support student learning, but the materials do not impose a uniform student-wide rule beyond instructor-specific course policies.",
        "evidence": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) can serve as a valuable tool for learning and completing academic tasks.\n\nSocratic is designed as a learning tool that will generate a conversational, human-like response with fun, unique graphics to help break down a particular concept. It’s a powerful studying tool that can help students check their homework or get across the last hurdle if a question or formula just isn’t making sense.\n\nJoin us for a dynamic 90-minute workshop designed for instructors looking to explore new ways to integrate AI into your classrooms to enhance student learning, boost engagement, and foster inclusivity. In this session, we will:\n  * Explore the potential uses of AI for students.\n  * Engage in discussions aimed at improving students’ overall learning experience through the integration of AI.",
        "sourceUrls": ["https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/elearningstudents/tools/ai-for-students/", "https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/elearningfaculty/ai-resources/", "https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/facultycommons/2024/09/09/improvestudentlearningwithai/"],
