        "summary": "Bellevue College provides faculty with AI detection tools as optional resources and notes that views differ on their effectiveness. Enforcement consequences for student misuse are not standardized in the provided materials; instead, faculty are encouraged to set course-specific consequences in their own AI and academic integrity policies.",
        "evidence": "There are various views about the effectiveness of AI detection tools. This is a list for faculty who choose to explore using the tools in their classrooms. All of these tools are free, or a free trial period is available to test them out.\n\nIn this self-paced, asynchronous workshop series, participants will discuss and determine how generative artificial intelligence should and/or should not be used by students and what the consequences for misuse should be. The ultimate goal of this workshop is for faculty to individually create policies on AI and academic integrity that are discipline-specific and can be added to course syllabi.\n\nIndividual classes and instructors will define their specific expectations regarding AI use, including whether it is permitted, the rationale for its use or restriction, and the consequences of inappropriate use.",
